  "heading": "\\function:?on{A}:?to{B}",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{function}\\textrm{ on }A\\textrm{ to }B\\quad\\htmlClass{mlg-title-written}{f \\: : \\: A \\rightarrow B}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\function:?on{A}:?to{B}]\nDefines: f(x__) ::= y_\nwhen: A, B is \\set\ndeclares:\n. x__ \"in\" A\n. y_ \"in\" B\nsatisfies:\n. forAll: x \"in\" A\n  then:\n  . existsUnique: y \"in\" B\n    suchThat: f(x) = y\nDocumented:\n. called: \"function@[A]{ on $A?$}@[B]{ to $B?}$\"\n. written: \"@[A, B]{f? \\: : \\: A? \\rightarrow B?}\"\n. description: \"A function $f : A \\rightarrow B$ assigns to each element $x$ of\n                the domain $A$ exactly one element $f(x)$ of the codomain $B$.\n                The defining requirement is existence and uniqueness of the\n                output: for every $x \\in A$ there is one and only one $y \\in B$\n                with $f(x) = y$.\"\nId: \"1e0cb28d-bc8f-42db-bcfa-86a215e88c7a\"",
